---
import BaseLayout
from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import me from "../content/images/me.jpg";
import me2 from "../content/images/me2.jpg";
import robots from "../content/images/robot_love.jpg";
import model from "../content/images/model.jpg";
---

<BaseLayout
title="Luke"
>

<section>

<div class="text">

<p>

I am an undergraduate student at the University of Michigan majoring in Math and Physics. My curiosities include robotics ethics, soft robotics, philosophy, theology, and complex systems.  
</p>

<br>
<p>
In the future, I intend to go to graduate school somewhere between Applied Math, Robotics, and Physics. Check back in a few years to find out my professional research interests.

</p>
<br>
<p>

I think it's important to study the interactions within our ever-complicated universe, and I believe the current wave of automation
crashing over society raises distinct questions about how we live "the good life." 
</p>
<br>
<p>
In particular, I've taken an interest in thinking about how automation might (or might not) introduce new moral agents onto the scene.
</p>


<p>
<br>
On this site, you can find my research experience and my writing as I reflect on things 
ethical, mathematical, Christian, and personal. 
</p>
<br>
<p>
Perhaps I'll even defend some positions along the way.
</p>
<br>

<figure>
  <Image src={model} alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;" } />
  <figcaption>"Γνώμη," in english meaning "Mind" or "Judgement," the page's favicon.
    May we all think as deeply.
  </figcaption>
</figure>


</div>

<aside>

<Image src={me} alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;" } />
<Image src={me2} alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;" } />
<figure>
<Image src={robots} alt="" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto;" } />
<figcaption>Robots hanging out.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

</aside>

</section>

</BaseLayout>

<style>

section {

display:

grid;

grid-template-columns:

2fr 240px;

gap:

60px;

}

.text {

font-family: "Bahn";

font-size:

1rem;

}

figcaption {
    padding:.6rem 1rem;
    color: var(--back);
    border: 2px solid var(--back);
    align:center
    
}

aside {

display:

flex;

flex-direction:

column;

gap:

10px;

}

.placeholder {



}

img {

width:

100%;

border:

4px solid var(--text);

}

</style>